{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "notes": [
    "Head values may be: a single label, a LIST of labels (set-valued / partial label: the truth is one of these, we do not know which), or omitted (= unknown; the head is ignored in the loss).",
    "Never map a coarse source label to a fine target label. E.g. binary 'rotten' says nothing about ripeness -> ripeness stays unknown.",
    "Path rules are regexes (Python re.search, case-insensitive) applied to the POSIX path relative to the dataset root. For each head, the FIRST matching rule wins.",
    "verified_against_download=false means the folder/column names come from the dataset paper/README and must be confirmed after download. The manifest builder fails on any file that yields no produce label (unless default_produce is set).",
    "produce.*.ripeness_visual: whether skin appearance carries ripeness evidence (docs/research/produce-science.md). strong | cultivar_dependent (ripeness enabled only with per-cultivar labels) | weak | not_applicable (ripeness head never enabled)."
  ],
  "unknown": "unknown",
  "heads": {
    "ripeness": ["unripe", "partially_ripe", "ripe", "overripe"],
    "freshness": ["fresh", "declining", "spoiled"],
    "visual_spoilage": ["none", "mild", "severe"]
  },
  "produce": {
    "banana":        {"category": "fruit", "he": "בננה", "emoji": "🍌", "priority": "P1", "ripeness_visual": "strong"},
    "apple":         {"category": "fruit", "he": "תפוח", "emoji": "🍎", "priority": "P1", "ripeness_visual": "not_applicable"},
